  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AWB Egypt  Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The most significant expected Project-level outcome is increased access to climate and SME finance. IFC anticipates that via market enabling and demonstration/replication channels, the Project is expected to increase the competitiveness of the SME and climate finance markets in Egypt and demonstrate the viability of supporting an underserved segment through the demonstration and replication channel in an environment of devaluations, challenging macro and global economic conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project involves an IFC investment of (i) a subordinated loan of up to US$20 million; and (ii) a US$10 million equivalent in local currency unfunded risk sharing facility (RSF) to support Attijariwafa Bank Egypt (AWBE or the Bank) lending program to small and medium enterprises (SMEs), for which IFCs maximum exposure will be up to 50% of an aggregate portfolio of a maximum amount of up to US$20 million (the Project).</narrative>
  </description>
